// endpoint_subscribe_github_merge_queue.proto — SubscribeGithubMergeQueue:
// tell one workspace's agent each time a repository branch's GITHUB merge
// queue moves: an entry joined, merged, or was removed, or the head changed.
// AGENT API section.
//
// TO FOLLOW ONE PULL REQUEST through its queue, subscribe to the pull request
// with PULL_REQUEST_NOTICE_EVENT_MERGE_QUEUE instead (an owned link already
// does). This rpc is for watching the whole queue.
//
// DELIVERY. Each notice (GithubMergeQueueNotice) is submitted to the
// subscriber's session as a deferred prompt of origin
// conversation.v1.PromptOrigin.PROMPT_ORIGIN_GITHUB_MERGE_QUEUE_NOTICE: it
// waits behind a running turn, wakes an idle agent, and the feed draws no row
// for it.
//
// NOTHING SLIPS BETWEEN READING AND FOLLOWING. The answer carries the queue
// as it stands when the subscription is taken, and every change after that
// read is told.
//
// SCOPE AND LIFETIME. A subscriber holds at most one subscription per queue;
// subscribing again is an answer (`already_subscribed`) that keeps what it
// was told. A subscription ends when the subscriber unsubscribes or closes
// however it closes. It is DURABLE across a daemon restart and a handover.

